<title>Cryptosporidiosis: Treatment.</title>
<graphic href="eee0301-w001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Cryptosporidiosis confirmed. Notify public health officials. Is patient immunocompromised?</label>
<path target="cell-2">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-3">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Type of immunocompromise.</label>
<path target="cell-4">HIV</path>
<path target="cell-5">Other causes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Maximized anti-HIV therapy and rehydration.</label>
<path target="cell-6"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>If patient is not responding, consider infectious disease consult. Nitazoxanide, Paromomycin. or azithromycin may improve symptoms and oocyte shedding, but may not cure.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Correct underlying cause of immunodeficiency, rehydration.</label>
<path target="cell-6"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Are symptoms severe or prolonged?</label>
<path target="cell-7">Mild/moderate symptoms</path>
<path target="cell-8">Severe/prolonged symptoms</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Symptomatic therapy with oral or IV rehydration. Nitazoxanide optional.</label>
<path target="cell-6"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Rehydration, nitazoxanide, and symptomatic therapy.</label>
<path target="cell-6"></path>
</cell>
</algorithm>
